@page "/keyboard"
<PageTitle>Keyboard scenarios · Blazor Accessibility Toolkit</PageTitle>

<div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Browser tests · Playwright</p>
    <h1>Keyboard scenarios</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Markup can be perfect while the behavior is broken: focus that never moves into a dialog, Escape that does
        nothing, errors that appear where nobody is looking. <code>BlazorTestHost</code> renders a single component with
        Interactive Server in a real browser, with in-process parameters. A <code>KeyboardScenario</code> then presses real
        keys and checks where focus goes.
    </p>
</div>

<RunAllTests />

<ul class="reasons">
    <li>Expectations poll until they hold or time out, so Blazor Server round trips need no fixed delays.</li>
    <li><code>Audit("state")</code> runs a full axe-core audit in the middle of the interaction.</li>
    <li>When a step fails, the error contains a transcript of every step and where focus was after it.</li>
</ul>

<section aria-labelledby="dialogs">
    <h2 id="dialogs">A modal dialog</h2>
    <p>
        Both dialogs have the same, valid markup: <code>role="dialog"</code>, <code>aria-modal="true"</code> and a name.
        A markup audit passes both. Only keyboard behavior tells them apart. Open each one with the keyboard and press
        Tab and Escape.
    </p>
    <ExampleCard Title="A dialog without focus management" Defect="true" Example="KeyboardExamples.FocuslessDialogScenario" Sources="@(["FocuslessDialog.razor"])"
                 Affects="@(["Keyboard users", "Screen reader users", "Screen magnifier users"])">
        <Stage>
            <FocuslessDialog TriggerText="Delete account" Title="Delete account?" ConfirmText="Delete">
                <p>This removes your profile and cannot be undone.</p>
            </FocuslessDialog>
        </Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
    <ExampleCard Title="A dialog that manages focus" Example="KeyboardExamples.ModalDialogScenario" Sources="@(["ModalDialog.razor"])">
        <ChildContent><p>Focus moves to Cancel, Tab stays inside, Escape closes it, and focus returns to the button that opened it.</p></ChildContent>
        <Stage>
            <ModalDialog TriggerText="Delete account" Title="Delete account?" ConfirmText="Delete">
                <p>This removes your profile and cannot be undone.</p>
            </ModalDialog>
        </Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="forms">
    <h2 id="forms">Form errors with the keyboard</h2>
    <p>
        After a failed submit, keyboard and screen reader users need focus on the first invalid field, and that field
        must describe the error. The test also reads the field's accessibility information: role, name, description and
        states, computed with axe-core's implementation of the accessible name algorithm.
    </p>
    <ExampleCard Title="The template form" Defect="true" Example="KeyboardExamples.LegacySignupScenario" Sources="@(["LegacySignupForm.razor"])"
                 Affects="@(["Keyboard users", "Screen reader users"])">
        <Stage><LegacySignupForm /></Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
    <ExampleCard Title="A form that moves focus to the first error" Example="KeyboardExamples.SignupScenario" Sources="@(["SignupForm.razor"])">
        <Stage><SignupForm /></Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
</section>

